Chapter: InductionListFalse
  cites Foreword chapter InductiveList

 The guard for the foreword-container induction half. A false claim inducted
 over the foreword's `IList` must be REJECTED, not warned about.

 This is the tripwire for the whole capability. Before
 `Foreword chapter InductiveList` existed, the only container a proof
 could induct over was one the file declared itself, and induction over
 a foreword container fell through to CDX4022 -- an unproven axiom, a
 warning, a compile that succeeds. `for all (xs : List Integer),
 5 === 6` compiles to this day for exactly that reason.

 So if this file ever starts compiling, the meaning is specific and
 bad: Stage 5 stopped resolving `IList` to a variant and went back to
 accepting anything inducted over it. The claim below is false --
 appending nil does not give nil -- and it must be a hard error.

Section: Bad Proof

  claim iappend-nil-false : for all (xs : IList Integer), ilist-append xs INil === INil
  proof iappend-nil-false =
   induction on xs
    is INil -> Refl
    is ICons (h) (t) (ih) -> cong ih
   qed

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni "unreachable"
  end
